WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.818
Spherical CNNs replace the plane with the sphere as
the domain of the signal,

00:00:04.898 --> 00:00:09.016
which is exactly right for data like molecules and
the atmosphere.

00:00:09.096 --> 00:00:12.959
The catch is that their core operation, spherical
convolution,

00:00:13.039 --> 00:00:15.503
is most accurate in the spectral domain,

00:00:15.583 --> 00:00:19.765
and that is far more expensive than an ordinary
planar convolution.

00:00:19.845 --> 00:00:23.772
Because of this cost, spherical CNNs had been
limited to small,

00:00:23.852 --> 00:00:27.016
low-resolution problems with modest model capacity.

00:00:27.096 --> 00:00:32.867
There simply was no large-scale spherical
architecture analogous to the deep planar networks

00:00:32.947 --> 00:00:35.030
that power modern computer vision.
